<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Why the application says this and not only the recorder.

    The recording is done by the localog-record-meeting sidecar, and that binary
    carries these same two strings linked into its own __info_plist. That is not
    enough. macOS attributes a request for the microphone or for system audio to
    the *responsible* process, and for a sidecar the application that spawned it
    is responsible. Without the strings here, the application asking on the
    sidecar's behalf has given no reason, and macOS answers a request with no
    reason by killing the process that made it.

    Tauri merges this file into the generated Info.plist when it bundles for
    macOS. Everything else in that file — identifier, version, minimum system —
    stays where it is, in tauri.conf.json.
  -->
  <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
  <string>LocaLog records the microphone so the people in the room can be transcribed. The recording and the transcription stay on this device.</string>
  <key>NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription</key>
  <string>LocaLog records what the meeting is playing so the people joining remotely can be transcribed too. The recording and the transcription stay on this device.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
